@startuml
title Repairing an under-covered repository

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

actor operator as OP
participant "jqa-verify-github" as VER
database "graph" as G
participant "run-jqa\n(github)" as JQA
database ".github-cache" as C
boundary "GitHub API" as GH

VER -> G : count per repository
VER -> GH : GraphQL totalCount
VER --> OP : under-covered: 1 of 261 issues

note over OP
  Each of the following steps is a NO-OP on its own.
  All three are required.
end note

OP -> G : 1. delete the GitHub subgraph of that repository
note right: otherwise jQAssistant skips the URI:\n"has already been scanned, skipping" (DEBUG level!)

OP -> C : 2. remove meta.json
note right: otherwise only items newer than lastScanAt are fetched --\na cache that started out partial never fills itself

OP -> JQA : 3. scan, restricted to that one URL
JQA -> GH : full fetch
GH --> JQA : 261 issues + 504 PRs
JQA -> G : write

OP -> VER : 4. verify again
VER --> OP : 261/261 -- 100%
@enduml
